# The prompt accepts offsets and day words: +3d, -2w, yesterday, 1d, 3 days, saving YYYY-MM-DD.
file <<END
- A
- B
- C
- D
- E
END
keys md
type +3d
keys <Enter> j md
type -2w
keys <Enter> j ms
type YESTERDAY
keys <Enter> j ms
type 1d
keys <Enter> j md
type 3 days
keys <Enter>
quit
saved <<END
- A @due({today+3})
- B @due({today-14})
- C @start({today-1})
- D @start({today+1})
- E @due({today+3})
END
